[gd_resource type="Theme" load_steps=25 format=3]

; Vanta Eclipse UI theme — red on black, minimal.
;
; Type is Nunito (SIL OFL): 900 for display, 800 for anything pressable, 700
; for body.
;
; MINIMAL IS A SHAPE DECISION, NOT A HUE ONE. The previous theme was "chunky
; neon": 28-32px radii, an 8px bottom lip on every button, and a coloured
; shadow at size 26-34 behind nearly everything. Recolouring that to red would
; have produced a red neon sign, not a minimal interface. So:
;   1. Radius drops 28 -> 6. Shapes are rectangles with the corner taken off,
;      not pills.
;   2. Every glow shadow is gone. The only shadow left is a black one under the
;      modal card, and it is there to separate layers, not to decorate.
;   3. The bottom lip is gone. A button is a flat fill or a 1px outline.
;   4. Space does the work the glow used to. Content margins stay generous.
;
; COLOUR is one accent and a true-neutral ramp. Not violet-tinted "near
; neutrals" — actually neutral, so the red is the only chroma in the chrome:
;   ink    #EDEDF0 on base  16.5:1
;   muted  #9C9CA5 on base   7.0:1
;   red    #FF3B30 on base   5.4:1   (marks, active state, small text)
;   white on #A8101A         7.6:1   (the filled primary button)
;
; The bright red and the deep red are two different jobs and are not
; interchangeable: #FF3B30 has to sit on black and be read, #A8101A has to sit
; UNDER white and be read. A single red cannot do both and clear 7:1 either way.
;
; Red is spent, not sprayed. It marks the primary action, the active state, and
; danger — and nothing else. Everything a player is not currently being asked to
; do is neutral. That restraint is most of what reads as "minimal"; the old
; theme put its accent on every border, every title and every pill at once.

[ext_resource type="FontFile" path="res://fonts/vanta_pixel.fnt" id="1"]
; The grabber is an ICON, not a stylebox — no StyleBox setting can reach it, so
; leaving it out means the engine default: a small pale dot with no relation to
; this palette.
[ext_resource type="Texture2D" path="res://sprites/ui/slider_grabber.png" id="4"]

